# This machine's own settings for the LocalLLM scripts: ~/.config/localllm/local.env (mode 600). Reference listing
# only creates one from this template if run standalone without a backup). It stays out of the repo, so where your backups and passphrase are isn't in it; the settings backup saves

# The file holding the backup passphrase (one line, mode 600). archive-backup.sh and the scheduled backup read it;
# without it, archive-backup.sh asks for the passphrase and the scheduled backup can't run.
# BACKUP_PASSPHRASE_FILE="$HOME/path/to/your/passphrase-file"

# Where archive-backup.sh keeps its encrypted archives (the newest BACKUP_KEEP_COUNT).
# BACKUP_ARCHIVE_DIR="$HOME/path/to/archive-folder"

# Where upload-backup.sh (and the scheduled backup) uploads them: an rclone remote and a folder in it, as
# remote:folder. Create the remote with `rclone config` first.
# BACKUP_REMOTE="your-remote:your-folder"
# How many encrypted archives to keep, in the archive folder and on the remote: the newest ones stay, older ones are
# deleted after each new backup. With the scheduled backup every 6 hours, 8 is about 2 days of PC use.
# BACKUP_KEEP_COUNT="8"

# The model: a profile in the repo's models/ folder (file name without .env); unset, the one named in models/default.
# After changing it: install/llama.sh (downloads it), install/pi.sh, then stop/llama.sh && start/llama.sh.
# MODEL_PROFILE="name-of-a-profile"

# GPU settings for llama.cpp:
# - LLAMA_CUDA_ARCH: the GPU generation install/llama.sh builds for (89 = RTX 40, 86 = RTX 30, 75 = RTX 20,
#   61 = GTX 10); unset, it's read from the GPU (nvidia-smi). A change rebuilds llama.cpp on the next install/llama.sh.
# - LLAMA_THREADS: CPU threads; unset, the number of physical cores.
# After changing them: stop/llama.sh && start/llama.sh.
# LLAMA_CUDA_ARCH="86"
# LLAMA_THREADS="8"
